  "id": "up-and-down-method",
  "term": "up-and-down method",
  "definition": "The up-and-down method is a dose-finding approach used to estimate the drug concentration needed to produce a target effect in a proportion of patients, such as the concentration that prevents coughing in 50% or 95% of people during emergence from anesthesia. In the source, it was used with isotonic regression to estimate effective remifentanil concentrations.",
